# Every box, Pi or x86 (MAD-846, ADR 0013). The platform lists add to it.

# Kiosk stack: cage (Wayland kiosk compositor), chromium, and color emoji
# for the room UI. Explicit DRI drivers so the GPU is usable by cage and
# Chromium (pulls in Mesa even if a chromium dependency change would not).
cage
chromium
fonts-noto-color-emoji
libgl1-mesa-dri

# mDNS: the box advertises <hostname>.local (set from name= in
# syncphony.txt), which the setup screen's QR code points phones at.
avahi-daemon

# The kiosk wrapper probes boxd with curl; boxd checks the server's
# /healthz (including over HTTPS) before the kiosk navigates.
curl
ca-certificates

# Audio stack: PipeWire with its PulseAudio compatibility layer. Chromium
# plays through pipewire-pulse, and audio-setup selects the sink with
# pactl (ADR 0004). alsa-utils: aplay for the hardware checklist.
pipewire
pipewire-bin
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pulseaudio-utils
alsa-utils

# Watchdogs (MAD-806, ADR 0008): a sane clock before the kiosk starts.
systemd-timesyncd

# HDMI-CEC (MAD-807, ADR 0009): cec-ctl talks to the kernel CEC framework.
v4l-utils

# The Wi-Fi setup hotspot (MAD-808, ADR 0010): NetworkManager runs the
# access point, and its shared mode needs dnsmasq-base for DHCP and DNS.
network-manager
dnsmasq-base
